{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"petite-dying-maggot","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nBedrock Converse `outputConfig` (native structured output) is rejected CLIENT-SIDE by the\ncurrently locked botocore 1.40.61 (`ParamValidationError` before any network call — measured,\nE1 experiment recorded on the selection bug ticket). The wire feature needs botocore >= 1.43.\nThe lock sits at 1.40.61 because of the declared extras diamond: `[eval]` -> inspect-ai ->\naioboto3 -> aiobotocore caps `boto3 < 1.40.62`, while `pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock]`\n(pyproject.toml:250) wants newer; the `[tool.uv]` conflicts block (pyproject.toml, ~line 261)\nalready forks eval vs bedrock/dev resolution to keep both installable.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd an explicit floor `botocore>=1.43.0` (and matching `boto3>=1.43.0`) alongside the\n`pydantic-ai-slim[bedrock]` dependency in pyproject.toml, then `uv lock`. Assumption stated as\ndefault: the existing conflict forks absorb the eval cap exactly as they do today (eval and\nbedrock never co-resolve); if the lock proves unresolvable, the fallback is scoping the floor\nto the bedrock-carrying extra only. No source change; the capability rows story is what makes\nthe new wire feature reachable — this ticket is purely the SDK floor.\n\nPurely mechanical dependency bump: no new testable behavior, so no Testing section (the\nexisting suite gates regressions).\n\n## Scope\n\n- pyproject.toml — the floor declaration\n- uv.lock — regenerated\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `uv lock` succeeds with the existing `[tool.uv]` conflicts block unchanged — checked by\n      the lock command exiting 0 in-session.\n- [ ] The dev/bedrock resolution contains botocore >= 1.43 — checked by `uv tree` (or\n      `uv pip list`) output recorded in the commit/ticket showing the resolved version.\n- [ ] The eval fork still resolves (`uv sync --extra eval` exits 0) — checked in-session.\n- [ ] `make test` passes on the new lock — checked by the CI-gating suite before push.","id":"531b-a5a7-91a2-4e4c","parent_id":"196d-28c4-ef0f-445c","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Raise the Bedrock SDK floor to botocore >= 1.43 for outputConfig"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785891867105643001,"uuid":"50dfe5e0-e927-40bb-bb00-8da8d8f4d893"}